SRB2Kart for LazyOS (the `org.lazy.srb2kart` package)
=====================================================

This package combines two works:

1. The game engine: SRB2Kart (Kart-Public v1.6, https://github.com/STJr/Kart-Public),
   by Kart Krew, derived from Sonic Robo Blast 2 by Sonic Team Junior, which
   derives from Doom Legacy (the Doom Legacy team), itself derived from id
   Software's Linux Doom source. Copyright (C) 1993-1996 id Software, Inc.;
   (C) 1998-2000 Doom Legacy team; (C) Sonic Team Junior; (C) Kart Krew.
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your
   option) any later version.

2. The LazyOS platform layer (`srb2kart/` in the LazyOS tree): the Rust program
   and C backend that implement the engine's platform hooks on the LazyOS
   display and input services. Licensed under the GNU General Public License,
   version 3 or (at your option) any later version.

   The engine is statically linked into `bin/srb2kart.elf`, so the binary as
   a whole is distributed under the GNU GPL, version 3 or later.

The game data is NOT part of this package and is NOT covered by the GPL. The
SRB2Kart v1.6 data files (`srb2.srb`, `*.kart`) are (C) Kart Krew. The image
build downloads them unmodified from Kart Krew's own release
(https://github.com/STJr/Kart-Public/releases/download/v1.6/AssetsLinuxOnly.zip)
and places them in /system/share/srb2kart; LazyOS does not redistribute them.
See `srb2kart/CREDITS.txt` (installed beside the data). Sonic the Hedgehog and
related characters are trademarks of SEGA. SRB2Kart is a fan game, not
affiliated with or endorsed by SEGA or Sonic Team.

Corresponding source
--------------------

The complete corresponding source of `bin/srb2kart.elf` is:

* the LazyOS tree at the revision this package was built from (`srb2kart/`,
  `xui-app/`, `libs/messenger/`, `libs/fhs/`, `libs/generated/`,
  `tools/srb2kart/`), and
* Kart-Public v1.6 (the source archive pinned by SHA-256 in
  `tools/srb2kart/fetch.py`), fetched unmodified and compiled by
  `srb2kart/build.rs` (any overlaid file is listed in `srb2kart/README.md`).

`python tools/srb2kart/build.py` rebuilds the package from those two sources.
The same source is available from whoever gave you this package, on request,
for at least three years.
